  "notes": "A する-verb from {遂行|すいこう}, a compound of {遂|すい} (accomplish, finally) and {行|こう} (perform). Formal and somewhat stiff; common in business, military, and official contexts. Emphasizes carrying a task through to completion.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive — takes を to mark the task being accomplished.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {任務|にんむ}を{遂行|すいこう}する — to carry out a mission\n- {職務|しょくむ}を{遂行|すいこう}する — to perform one's duties\n- {計画|けいかく}を{遂行|すいこう}する — to execute a plan\n- {作戦|さくせん}を{遂行|すいこう}する — to carry out an operation\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {実行|じっこう}する — to execute, to carry out (more general, less formal)\n- {履行|りこう}する — to fulfill (specifically obligations and contracts)\n- {達成|たっせい}する — to achieve, to accomplish (focuses on reaching a goal)",
